  "problem": "A study shows how the sports preferences of young people in a certain community vary from year to year. The following table shows the results of this study. \n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Basketball</b></td> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Football</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"60\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Football</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFor example, $10%$ of people who used to prefer baseball now prefer football. \n\nGiven that $1\\,260$ young people were interviewed for the study and that the probabilities listed remain constant for many years, how many of those people will eventually prefer baseball?",
